# CODEOWNERS
#
# CODEOWNERS defines who must review changes to different parts of the repo.
# GitHub automatically adds these reviewers to any PR that touches matching files.
#
# RULES:
#   - More specific patterns (deeper paths) override broader patterns.
#   - The last matching rule wins.
#   - Teams must be created in GitHub Org settings before they can be referenced.
#   - Replace @your-org/* with your actual GitHub organisation and team slugs.
#
# DOCS: https://docs.github.com/en/repositories/managing-your-repositorys-settings-and-features/customizing-your-repository/about-code-owners

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Default owner — catches everything not matched by a more specific rule below.
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*                                       @your-org/ml-platform-team

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# CI / CD pipelines
# Any change to a GitHub Actions workflow must be reviewed by the platform team.
# This prevents accidental introduction of supply-chain risks.
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.github/                                @your-org/ml-platform-team
ci/                                     @your-org/ml-platform-team

# The shared security scan is extra-sensitive — require two teams.
ci/github-actions/_shared/              @your-org/ml-platform-team @your-org/security-team

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Infrastructure / Terraform
# Cloud resource changes require the platform infra team.
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
terraform/                              @your-org/platform-infra-team
terraform/gpu-cluster/                  @your-org/platform-infra-team @your-org/ml-platform-team

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Serving infrastructure
# Changes to serving configs affect production model latency and availability.
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
serving/                                @your-org/ml-platform-team
serving/vllm/                           @your-org/ml-platform-team @your-org/ml-engineers

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Monitoring
# Drift thresholds and alert rules directly affect retraining decisions.
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
monitoring/                             @your-org/ml-platform-team
monitoring/alerts/                      @your-org/ml-platform-team @your-org/sre-team
monitoring/dashboards/                  @your-org/ml-platform-team

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Policy & Governance
# Policy changes must be reviewed by the governance/legal team and ML platform.
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
policy/                                 @your-org/ml-governance-team @your-org/ml-platform-team
policy/data-governance/                 @your-org/ml-governance-team @your-org/data-protection-officer
policy/model-approval/                  @your-org/ml-governance-team @your-org/ml-platform-team

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# MLflow Tracking Server
# Any authentication or storage changes are security-sensitive.
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
mlflow/                                 @your-org/ml-platform-team

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# DVC pipeline templates
# Changes here affect reproducibility of all training runs.
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
dvc/                                    @your-org/ml-platform-team @your-org/ml-engineers

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Architecture Decision Records
# ADRs must be reviewed by architects — they record permanent design decisions.
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
docs/decisions/                         @your-org/ml-architects @your-org/ml-platform-team

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Golden paths and guides
# Documentation changes reviewed by the team that owns the topic.
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
docs/golden-paths/                      @your-org/ml-platform-team
docs/guides/                            @your-org/ml-platform-team
GETTING_STARTED.md                      @your-org/ml-platform-team
README.md                               @your-org/ml-platform-team

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Repository intelligence (.ai/)
# These files guide AI assistants. Changes affect all future AI-assisted work.
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.ai/                                    @your-org/ml-architects @your-org/ml-platform-team

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Pre-commit and developer tooling
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.pre-commit-config.yaml                 @your-org/ml-platform-team
Makefile                                @your-org/ml-platform-team
Taskfile.yml                            @your-org/ml-platform-team
.devcontainer/                          @your-org/ml-platform-team
